<section>
	<h1>About the App</h1>
	<p>
		<strong>Do Later</strong> is a minimalist to-do list built to stay out of your way. Jot down what you need to
		do, reorder it however you like, and check things off - without ads, accounts, or clutter.
	</p>
	<p>
		Beyond simple tasks, Do Later includes <strong>task generators</strong>: recurring rules that automatically add
		a task to your list on the days you choose. Set up "Take out the trash" every Tuesday or "Pay rent" on the 1st
		of each month, and the task appears on its own when the day arrives.
	</p>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Features</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Minimalist, distraction-free interface</li>
		<li>Recurring task generators (daily, weekly, monthly, or yearly)</li>
		<li>Sort tasks by age, name, or your own custom order</li>
		<li>Separate tab for completed tasks</li>
		<li>Light and dark themes, with optional compact rows</li>
		<li>Swipe to complete or delete</li>
		<li>Always free: 100% ad-free, no sign-in, no subscriptions</li>
		<li>Private: all data lives on your device - nothing is ever transmitted or retained</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>System Requirements</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>iPhone running a recent version of iOS</li>
		<li>Offline-only: all data stays on your device</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
	<dl>
		<dt>How do I add a new task?</dt>
		<dd>Tap the <strong>+</strong> button on the List tab, enter your task, and hit Save.</dd>

		<dt>How do I complete or delete a task?</dt>
		<dd>Swipe a task right to complete it or left to delete it. You can change these gestures in Settings.</dd>

		<dt>What is a task generator?</dt>
		<dd>
			A generator is a recurring rule that adds a task to your list automatically on a schedule you set - for
			example, every week on Monday, or on the last day of each month. Manage them on the <em>Generators</em> tab.
		</dd>

		<dt>How do I reorder my tasks?</dt>
		<dd>Set the sort mode to <em>Custom</em>, then drag tasks into the order you want.</dd>

		<dt>Where is my data stored?</dt>
		<dd>
			All data is stored locally on your device and is not accessible anywhere else. If you delete the app, all
			data is lost.
		</dd>
	</dl>
</section>

